Keep a --config path over the frontend default config path

config_set_defaults() runs after the first argument pass and sets
RARCH_PATH_CONFIG from g_defaults.path_config whenever the frontend filled
that in. The QNX frontend does (<cwd>/rarch-shared/retroarch.cfg), so
--config was always replaced and RetroArch said "Config not found" for its
own default. Only use the default when no path was given.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/configuration.c
+++ b/configuration.c
@@ -2968,7 +2968,11 @@
             g_defaults.dirs[DEFAULT_DIR_RECORD_CONFIG],
             sizeof(recording_st->config_dir));
 
-   if (!string_is_empty(g_defaults.path_config))
+   /* A frontend default (the QNX frontend sets one) must not replace a
+    * config file given with --config, which the first argument pass has
+    * already stored. */
+   if (!string_is_empty(g_defaults.path_config)
+         && path_is_empty(RARCH_PATH_CONFIG))
    {
       char temp_str[PATH_MAX_LENGTH];
 
